\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Structural geometry of \textit  {PSEN1} HL1 in PDB 6IYC, ESM-2 fold-tolerance scoring on Apple Silicon MPS, and thermodynamic design of allele-selective steric ASOs. \textbf  {(A)} Heavy-atom proximity of \textit  {PSEN1} HL1 residues (Chain B, 104--125) to APP-C83 (Chain E, solid navy) and nicastrin (Chain A, dashed teal), highlighting the 14.0\,\r A\ R108--I114 span excised by p.K109\_L113del (pink shading). \textbf  {(B)} Full-length ESM-2 (\texttt  {esm2\_t12\_35M\_UR50D}) embedding L2 perturbation showing that \textit  {PSEN1} p.K109\_L113del (0.0769, red) falls in the 5th percentile relative to 20 random 5-aa \textit  {PSEN1} internal deletions ($0.1039 \pm 0.0236$), consistent with preserved global folding. \textbf  {(C)} AlphaGenome splicing attribution plotted against SantaLucia nearest-neighbor allele selectivity ($\Delta \Delta G^\circ _{37} = \Delta G_{\text  {WT}} - \Delta G_{\text  {mut}}$) across 32 splice-hotspot targets, separating candidates avoiding canonical \texttt  {+1/+2\,GU} donors (dark blue; lead \textit  {PSEN1} p.K109* in red) from off-target GU-overlapping oligos (gray).}}{9}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fig4}{{4}{9}{Structural geometry of \textit {PSEN1} HL1 in PDB 6IYC, ESM-2 fold-tolerance scoring on Apple Silicon MPS, and thermodynamic design of allele-selective steric ASOs. \textbf {(A)} Heavy-atom proximity of \textit {PSEN1} HL1 residues (Chain B, 104--125) to APP-C83 (Chain E, solid navy) and nicastrin (Chain A, dashed teal), highlighting the 14.0\,\AA \ R108--I114 span excised by p.K109\_L113del (pink shading). \textbf {(B)} Full-length ESM-2 (\texttt {esm2\_t12\_35M\_UR50D}) embedding L2 perturbation showing that \textit {PSEN1} p.K109\_L113del (0.0769, red) falls in the 5th percentile relative to 20 random 5-aa \textit {PSEN1} internal deletions ($0.1039 \pm 0.0236$), consistent with preserved global folding. \textbf {(C)} AlphaGenome splicing attribution plotted against SantaLucia nearest-neighbor allele selectivity ($\Delta \Delta G^\circ _{37} = \Delta G_{\text {WT}} - \Delta G_{\text {mut}}$) across 32 splice-hotspot targets, separating candidates avoiding canonical \texttt {+1/+2\,GU} donors (dark blue; lead \textit {PSEN1} p.K109* in red) from off-target GU-overlapping oligos (gray)}{figure.4}{}}
